  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DANIDA SPA 2022 Turkey</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Vulnerable populations linked to the Syrian crisis have improved access to rights and entitlements through legal aid and specialised protection services   
Protection and legal information dissemination; Specialised Protection Services; Partnerships and Capacity Building 
- Improved self-reliance and resilience for host and Syrian refugee populations in the Middle East region through enhanced access to markets, and decent sustainable livelihoods in both urban and rural settings
Support to home-based businesses and MSMEs to provide decent and resilient livelihoods
- In the Middle East, local civil society have stronger capacity to coordinate, articulate, and advocate for durable solutions for those displaced by the Syrian crisis
- People in the Middle East benefit from programmes more aligned with existing institutions, markets and state support systems, including safety nets and social protection systems, based on evidence for more effective sustainable solutions across the humanitarian development nexus</narrative>
  </description>
